## How It Works

### Technical Deep Dive

#### Backend Architecture

The backend is a **FastAPI application** with fully **async architecture**:

```python
# Main entry point: backend/app/main.py
app = FastAPI(
    title="Beacon AI",
    version="5.0.0",
    description="Admin-grade Anti-Corruption Reporting System",
    lifespan=lifespan,  # Handles startup/shutdown
)
```

**Key Design Patterns:**
- **Lifespan management** — Database initialized on startup, cleaned on shutdown
- **Async everywhere** — All DB calls use `async/await` via SQLAlchemy 2.0
- **Dependency injection** — Database sessions are injected via FastAPI `Depends()`
- **Background tasks** — Post-submission AI analysis runs asynchronously

---

#### API Versioning and Route Structure

All APIs are versioned under `/api/v1/`:

```
/api/v1/
├── public/                  # No authentication required
│   ├── reports/
│   │   ├── create           # Start a new session
│   │   └── message          # Send a chat message
│   ├── evidence/
│   │   └── upload           # Upload files
│   └── track                # Track case status
│       ├── POST /track      # Verify Case ID + Secret Key
│       ├── POST /track/message  # Send follow-up message
│       └── POST /track/upload   # Upload attachment
│
├── admin/                   # JWT authentication required
│   ├── auth/login           # Admin login
│   └── reports/
│       ├── GET /            # List all cases
│       ├── GET /{id}        # Get case detail
│       ├── PUT /{id}/status # Update status
│       ├── POST /{id}/update  # Publish update
│       ├── POST /{id}/message # Send message
│       ├── POST /{id}/upload  # Upload attachment
│       └── POST /{id}/analyze # Re-trigger scoring
```

---

